end_lines.plain, line 4: Write "stop the program" instead.

        end the game
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try this:
        stop the program
Why: To Plain, a line that starts with "end" only marks where steps end, like "end if". To finish the program, Plain says "stop the program".

end_lines.plain, line 8: Write "stop repeating" instead.

        end repeating
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try this:
        stop repeating
Why: To Plain, a line that starts with "end" only marks where steps end, like "end repeat". To leave the repeat, Plain says "stop repeating".

end_lines.plain, line 12: Delete this line, or write "end repeat" instead.

    end for
    ^^^^^^^
Try this:
    end repeat
Why: Plain knows only "end", "end if", "end repeat" and "end try", and it doesn't need them. It goes by how far each line is moved to the right.

